{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122554-tremere-2e-homebrew","id":1122554,"title":"Tremere 2e Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-29T18:02:21-07:00","id":1122554,"title":"Tremere 2e Homebrew","content":"I am working on a 2e version of the Tremere, based on what's in the 1st edition core book, Left-Hand Path, and the scant few notes about the actual 2e rules that have been released.<br /> <br /> The document is <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1DB-myfiG0ojvEMIRlobsJZAl6wqirJZXJbX6sKr2JGg/pub?embedded=true\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. I absolutely consider this a rough draft, nowhere near ready for playtesting yet. I am mostly looking for comments on the practicality and balance of the rules. I expect the idea to go through several revisions, potentially bordering on complete rewrites.<br /> <br /> In short: The Tremere harvest souls to fuel their immortality and strange powers. Instead of Gnosis, they have Hollow. Hollow is much more variable than Gnosis, and while Tremere at Hollow 10 are very powerful, they can be consumed by the the living void of the Final Watchtower if they are not careful. Tremere liches manage their power in cycles, ramping up their connection to the Watchtower over a few years (or months) to perform powerful feats of magic with their Call of the Void ability, before going into the mystical sleep of death to regain some sense of self.<br /> <br /> The powers are based off of what's in 1e, plus my own inspiration. I've explicitly moved away from the Tremere being a Death-based legacy with these rules. Instead, my idea is to characterize the Tremere as eternal searchers seeking to achieve complete dominion over all five subtle Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 07-30-2017, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T04:25:28-07:00","id":1122665,"title":"","content":"I like what I'm reading so far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's much more involved and complicated that the simple modification I made for my own game.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You've written that Tremere gain one extra Praxis per dot of Hollow.<br /> How does that interact with losing Hollow? Do they lose the praxis? When they regain Hollow, can they pick a different praxis?<br /> <br /> Under the </span></span>Koimaomai section there seems to be a bit missing? &quot;Iflosin&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How do you succeed on a Hollow roll? Just get one success?<br /> Can a mage in </span></span>Koimaomai spend that time wandering the Astral? Being awake, but a corpse seems rather boring. Could the Tremere Possess someone?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T04:33:45-07:00","id":1122667,"title":"","content":"Currently I have this regarding losing Hollow: &quot;If the lich would not have enough Hollow to access Hollow Attainments or Hollow Praxes, then they do not lose the abilities themselves; they just lose access until their Hollow increases enough again. When losing access to Praxes, the lich chooses which ones to lose.&quot; So they don't lose the Praxis itself, they just lose access to it, although they can pick which one(s) they lose access to when dropping Hollow.<br /> <br /> Don't see the &quot;Iflosin&quot; part in the koimaomai section. Might be a typo I fixed?<br /> <br /> The Hollow roll requires 1 success, yes.<br /> <br /> The actions during koimaomai part comes from Left-Hand Path, which says &quot;typically, spells that provide extrasensory perception or a way to travel outside the body.&quot; So yes, it would seem that going on Astral journeys or otherwise traveling without your body would be one of the intended uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T06:47:11-07:00","id":1122687,"title":"","content":"I've updated the document to include the House rules, along with a port of House Nagaraja and House Heo Sel. I will add Houes Thrax and House Vedmak soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:34:55-07:00","id":1123919,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;The Attainments of House Khentamenti are based around commanding the powers of Death. They are inspired by/taken from the optional Attainment effects of Left-Hand Path.&quot;<br /> <br /> On what page the The Left Hand Path do I find these optional Attainments?<br /> <br /> <br /> House Thrax seems to have a lot of bookkeeping regarding the skills of people who's souls have been stolen.<br /> <br /> Regarding the 3rd Attainment, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Legion\u2019s Discipline (Life 3)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do the victims need to be alive for the attainment to work?<br /> Is the skill &quot;stored&quot; in the soul or the person? When they die, does the Tremere lose access to the skill because the person who had the skill is dead.<br /> Note being a soulless Thrall is not a death sentence, it comes with the Broken Condition attached making a Thrall unable to spend willpower and suck at combat and have -2 to social rolls.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":". 08-02-2017, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T12:58:53-07:00","id":1123982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122554-tremere-2e-homebrew?p=1123919#post1123919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;The Attainments of House Khentamenti are based around commanding the powers of Death. They are inspired by/taken from the optional Attainment effects of Left-Hand Path.&quot;<br /> <br /> On what page the The Left Hand Path do I find these optional Attainments?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> <br /> House Khentamenti is completely homebrew, and I'm still working on it. It's meant to be a home for the other Tremere Legacy Attainment effects that were discarded. I guess those are actually in the 1st edition Core Book. The flurry of creativity and the rules for the Tremere being in two books seems to have scattered my brains a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> House Thrax seems to have a lot of bookkeeping regarding the skills of people who's souls have been stolen.<br /> <br /> Regarding the 3rd Attainment, </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Legion\u2019s Discipline (Life 3)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do the victims need to be alive for the attainment to work?<br /> Is the skill &quot;stored&quot; in the soul or the person? When they die, does the Tremere lose access to the skill because the person who had the skill is dead.<br /> Note being a soulless Thrall is not a death sentence, it comes with the Broken Condition attached making a Thrall unable to spend willpower and suck at combat and have -2 to social rolls.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>These are good points, and are exactly what I'm looking for in feedback. The idea for the Thrax was inspired by the Cloud Infinite Legacy in Left-Hand Path, which is similar in a way, although probably with less bookkeeping. Ideally I'd prefer to keep bookkeeping to a minimum. Honestly, if I was the ST in that situation, I'd just make up stats on the fly when the Tremere player requested them. I will try to think of ways to keep the &quot;legion feel,&quot; but with less bookkeeping. At most I would want a Thrax player to keep track of the number of souls they have, and <i>maybe</i> their relative strengths, on a broad level (e.g. &quot;I have 5 strong souls, 2 mediocre ones, and 3 weak ones&quot;). <br /> <br /> As for souls and the death of the owners, I'm not sure this is addressed even in first edition. House Heo Sel has a similar situation with Crafts from the Grim Hall. If they can use the soul's owner's Skill with their created tool, what happens when the owner dies? I'm inclined to say that even if the soul's owner is dead, the relevant dots persist--at least for some time. Perhaps it starts to decay after a while?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:27:36-07:00","id":1124034,"title":"","content":"There's no reason to assume that a person's soul departs upon their death if they've been separated from it. Souls being used by Tremere tend to degrade because they're being consumed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T16:10:56-07:00","id":1124058,"title":"","content":"Well in this case it's more about the mystical relation between the soul's owner and the soul itself. If souls are the &quot;vessel&quot; for a mage's Gnosis, it's probably the same even for Sleepers. Their experiences and lives shape their souls. So in that case it'd be reasonable to assume that relevant dots in Skills or Attributes remain even if the soul's owner dies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:31:41-07:00","id":1128190,"title":"","content":"From what I have read I have trouble understanding why would Tremere reduce their Hollow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T23:45:35-07:00","id":1128346,"title":"","content":"Great work, Projectmoon!<br /> As it stands, I only have one criticism; it seems like Houses offer so little considering how much they impose in the way of weaknesses.<br /> I suppose this is an issue arising from Left-Hand Path, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T06:07:05-07:00","id":1128409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122554-tremere-2e-homebrew?p=1128190#post1128190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I have read I have trouble understanding why would Tremere reduce their Hollow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Currently, there is a sort of magical &quot;safe number&quot; for Hollow around 6 or 7 where it's fairly powerful but also not very dangerous. At 8 and then again at 10 it becomes more dangerous, but only if the Call of the Void Yantra is used. The main driver for Call of the Void's danger is that you get beats when using it at high Hollow. I would like to resolve this safe area problem somehow. I'm thinking about detaching a lot of the scaling benefit from Call of the Void, so that it's just a regular +1 to +3 Yantra, and then shifting the benefits of high Hollow elsewhere. Problems: I don't know where to shift it, and it doesn't really solve the safe space problem (if anything, it makes it worse).<br /> <br /> Much of the danger from high Hollow is also supposed to be story-based. The local Consilium will probably take notice once a bunch of souls start going missing when the high-Hollow Tremere is slurping them up by the bucketload.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Great work, Projectmoon!</span> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">As it stands, I only have one criticism; it seems like Houses offer so little considering how much they impose in the way of weaknesses.<br /> I suppose this is an issue arising from Left-Hand Path, really.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> This is part of why I added the House Boon. I have ported most of the other stuff directly, including the need to eat more souls. Depending on what I do with Hollow, I may remove that requirement, as it doesn't really add anything except make it more annoying to be a Tremere.</span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:13:53-07:00","id":1129308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main driver for Call of the Void's danger </div> </div> </div>I read that Yantra. It may cause Hollowed condition involuntarily (if Tremere fails Resolve + Composure, which are high in most mages and may be boosted with magic), which can be shaken with Resolve + Composure again after one scene. That's pretty minor drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T15:12:56-07:00","id":1129451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122554-tremere-2e-homebrew?p=1129308#post1129308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read that Yantra. It may cause Hollowed condition involuntarily (if Tremere fails Resolve + Composure, which are high in most mages and may be boosted with magic), which can be shaken with Resolve + Composure again after one scene. That's pretty minor drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the time I wrote that, it worked differently. But the feedback for the new ability is also useful. The intent for the Resolve + Composure roll was to disallow magical bonuses, although I didn't state that anywhere yet. I'm also considering increasing the time it lasts, on a sliding scale. The Hollowed Condition itself is dangerous (albeit powerful) because of the Wisdom violations and additional Rampant Condition. Perhaps shifting it to a different type of roll would work. Maybe even inverting it like a Paradox roll? If the Tremere has to roll Hollow, and a success triggers the Hollowed state, it becomes far more likely to enter the Hollowed state when you are rolling 8-10 dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T07:21:08-07:00","id":1130239,"title":"","content":"Edit: Nevermind, I figured out the answer to my question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 08-17-2017, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:39:52-07:00","id":1130493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122554-tremere-2e-homebrew?p=1130239#post1130239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Nevermind, I figured out the answer to my question.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Out of curiosity, what was the question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:34:37-07:00","id":1130612,"title":"","content":"I was a bit confused about when Stave Off Annihilation would actually work, but then I noticed that you can get the Degraded condition when you've still got a soul in you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T09:01:22-07:00","id":1135171,"title":"","content":"The Tremere rules are now on iteration 26. I've been working a lot to condense the text, centralize rules, and remove things that don't really add to the experience. It is getting closer to a final draft.<br /> <br /> I've moved Koimaomai, Hollowed, and even &quot;being animated by an Awakened soul&quot; into Conditions to condense their rules.The Yantra bonus from Hollowed still remains, but it now scales with subtle Arcana AND Hollow.<br /> <br /> The next thing I will investigate is the Hollow Attainments, especially the last one. I'm not sure the highest level Hollow Attainment should just be a fancy soul jar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T06:40:42-07:00","id":1135419,"title":"","content":"Very interesting writeup! Side question: from a setting standpoint if you wanted to use the Tremere again in Vampire would you approach that from the perspective of a parallel development of &quot;Tremere&quot;, or splinter group of this Legacy who seeks a source of energy not tied to the distilled life-force of souls? (And which is therefore limited to the natural rate of soul generation and refinement.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:26:46-07:00","id":1135481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122554-tremere-2e-homebrew?p=1135419#post1135419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very interesting writeup! Side question: from a setting standpoint if you wanted to use the Tremere again in Vampire would you approach that from the perspective of a parallel development of &quot;Tremere&quot;, or splinter group of this Legacy who seeks a source of energy not tied to the distilled life-force of souls? (And which is therefore limited to the natural rate of soul generation and refinement.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>This version of the Tremere was not really designed with the whole &quot;Theban captivity&quot; idea in mind. In my head-canon, these Tremere stumbled upon their truth of the soul in any number of ways, possibly multiple ways given how dwellers in the Supernal can rewrite history. Tremere is/was/could have been a mage who Ascended, almost Ascended, or just barely escaped the Time Before, or even a conglomeration of people that coalesced into one legendary person over time that delivered the secret of the Final Watchtower. Or maybe it was never a person at all. Perhaps the Final Watchtower forced itself out of the Abyss into the Fallen World and touched the first liches.<br /> <br /> In that head-canon, the &quot;breath-eaters&quot; would probably be a conquered Reaper Legacy of the Tremere. That Legacy's history records the Theban Captivity, and their Attainments would focus around stealing the &quot;breath&quot; (souls) of people. These mages would have been interesting to the Tremere because they have Reaper-like powers, but don't seem to actually steal people's souls. Not to mention the connection to vampirism. The House in modern times would be full of innovative Attainments based on the original Legacy. They would by far have one of the weirdest sets of House Attainments. They would be a House that explores the Supernal concepts behind vampirism.<br /> <br /> The breath-eaters could also be some Tremere transformation gone awry, like the Preta. in that case, they would be a parallel development of sorts, but still connected to the main Order. Perhaps an enterprising Kindred elder got his hands on a would-be Tremere before they could complete the initiation. Elder attempts to Embrace the soulless initiate, and you get something weird instead. You could consider them a minor template of the Tremere, maybe? You could even weave them into the original idea: some time in history, a kindred elder (the Theban?) accidentally created some weird half vampire/half mages in the way described in this paragraph. The Tremere later absorbed this transformation as a new House, with the weird Attainments and focus described in the first paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 08-30-2017, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T14:52:53-08:00","id":1164071,"title":"","content":"I have added a first draft of House Samedi, a House dedicated to interweaving Spirit and souls. I think it needs some work, though. I'm not sure about the first two Attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T15:50:26-08:00","id":1167168,"title":"","content":"The Tremere have been updated again, quite heavily. First, House Khentamenti and House Samedi are finished.Second, the power of the Tremere has been toned down quite a bit. Conversely, their drawbacks are less. It is also much cheaper to increase Hollow quickly, and while advantageous to do so, it's nowhere near as powerful as it used to be. I also removed the degradation mechanic, and made the Tremere suffer soul loss normally, but it is much more dangerous for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T19:39:47-08:00","id":1167819,"title":"","content":"<br /> Hey ! Basically, I adore your take on the Tremere (the mechanics are elegant, and their new status of being beyond the Supernal divisions of the Arcana is just mindblowing).<br /> <br /> I'm currently trying to elaborate Houses for Arcana that have not yet a Tremere House specialized in them, and I thought it would be interesting to share it here. I may edit this post if I manage to wrap it up, but I'm not sure I will have the time, but I'd very much like to get some feedback about the way these Houses can incorporate Soul-Magic in their Attainments (I feel like I've skipped the problem by making &quot;normal&quot; Legacies Attainements, which is not half as interesting as exploring the Art of the Liches).<br /> <div align=\"center\"><u>HOMEBREW HOUSES</u></div> <br /> <br /> <b><u>House Xolotl </u></b><br /> Xolotl was the Aztec deity of death and lightning: a grim figure, with the face of a rabid hound, a flayed body, and feet pointed backwards: its priests knew how to diffract the Souls of human sacrifices in waves of pure energy, When the Conquistadors came and sacked Tenochtitlan, the few surviving members of the clergy received no less than three offers, from each of the European Awakened Sects. The Pentacle offered them shelter and peerage, if they gave up on their Reaping ways. The Seers offered them inclusion within the New Occidental Order, at the cost of enslavement. The Tremere simply offered revenge. And Xolotl\u2019s children chose revenge.<br /> <br /> <b>House Boon</b>: None of Nature\u2019s accesses of fury is unknown to Xolotl\u2019s devotees: they revel in storms and earthquakes, and dance amongst the ruins left by men. As long as they maintain the Hollowed state, Xolotl Liches can turn spend one Mana to convert any maluses stemming from environmental Conditions or Tilts, up to an Extreme Environment level of half their Hollow (rounded up) into bonuses.<br /> <br /> <b>House Weakness: </b>Impatient like a rabid dog, touchy as if their nerves were laid bare, and clumsy as if their limbs were switched: indeed, Xolotl\u2019s servants are a living (or unliving) portrayal of their god. They add five to the target success number of every extended or teamwork action they\u2019re involved in (even magical ones, like Scrutiny, Supernal Summoning or entering the Astral). Also, they\u2019re considered as having two less Doors than they should normally have in Social Maneuvering.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment; Whims of Tlaloc (Control Weather +2R)</b><br /> <b>Fourth Attainment: Rattling of the Tzitzimime (Influence Sound +3 R</b><br /> <b>Fifth Attainment: Fires of Xibalba (effect about Soul-consuming Flames)</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Prime : House Israfil</u></b><br /> Founded and mostly attended by former Obrimos with a monotheistic worldview, the House Israfil forms peaceful Angels of Death: not fighters, but able to resolve any fight nonetheless. They believe that by reaping Souls, they further the rebirth of the One Soul of the Fallen World \u2013 whether they name it Sophia, Schekhinah, or Khwajah-al-Akbar: in turn, that Soul shines like a halo on their brow, allowing them to perform miracles through the Souls they freed.<br /> <br /> <b>House Boon</b>: An Israfil maintaining the Hollowed Condition may add half his dots in Prime (rounded up) to any of his Arcana rating for the purpose Mage Armor. If he\u2019s also suffused by the Supreme Coin, he may forego this benefit and activate <i>two</i> different Mage Armors in the same Scene. (However, the Awakened Soul is destroyed at the end of the Scene).<br /> <br /> <b>House Weakness</b>: If all magic stems from the Divine, how could an Israfil try to evade its effects without transgressing God\u2019s will? Israfil Liches suffer a -2 penalty to Clashes of Wills and all non-Physical-based resistance rolls against Spells and other supernatural effects targeting him. Further, they gain the Spooked Condition if they witness or are targeted by a successful Spell garnering more successes than their Ego.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment: Gerasa (Dispellation: Instant Casting, Lasting)</b><br /> Just like Jesus banished the Legion of demons who took over the Gerasene and ordered them to enter the mind of swines, the Israfil seizes the wretched, divided magic of the Awakened and seal it within the lesser souls he harvested.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment: Gethsemane (Words of Power: Instant Casting, Sensory Range, Condition-Inducing) </b>All the apostles fell asleep between the olive trees of Gethsemane, for none was fit to bear the inner agony of the Christ, already conscious of his nearing death. Drawing upon the echo of those words, the Israfil states his own objective in objectively true terms.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment: Armageddon (Display of Power: Counterspell made easier, Instant Casting)</b><br /> The Israfil\u2019s Nimbus flares impossibly wide, forming three sets of radiant wings who deploy and circle the zone he\u2019s in, trapping up to twenty of his foes in a blank landscape illuminated by their eerie light. A Duel Arcane has begun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Space: House Carcosa </u></b><br /> <br /> <b>House Boon:</b> While they maintain the Hollow Condition, Carcosa Liche\u2019s Sympathetic Connection to anyone whose face they have seen at least once and who\u2019s currently under a Mental Condition is raised by one step (two if the Condition is a Persistent one).<br /> <br /> <b>House Weakness</b>: Each Carcosa Lich is a replica of the Dement City, and brings it in his wake: that makes them quite easy to follow, as their trails becomes hallways, traces of their presence shine like signposts, and all roads bend to lead to them. They\u2019re permanently under the Easy Prey Condition. Further, they must expend one additional Mana to magically affect any material used to restrain them physically \u2013 be it cuffs, cell walls, or even the flesh of a being Grappling them.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment: Have You Seen The Yellow Sign? (Scrying, Instant Casting, Sensory, Remote Casting)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment: Behind the Pallid Mask (Perfect Sympathy, Medium Connections, Fool Magic)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment: Rip the Tatters of the King (Borrow Threads, Instant Casting, Sensory, Remote)</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 08-20-2019, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T01:32:43-08:00","id":1167851,"title":"","content":"Most of the Attainments from first edition seemed to be modified versions of spells that could make use of benefit the soul's owner had, or was otherwise linked to the soul. The third Attainment of House Israfil could use the Arcana ratings of a soul in place of the mage's own, for example. But keep in mind, the House Attainments follow the rules for Legacy Attainments. So the dispellation Attainment would require the mage to touch the target (which may be hard, if it's an area spell). In general, the Prime and Space Attainments seem easier to work souls into. The first House that controls the weather is a bit more difficult for me. Some Tremere Attainments don't have to directly utilize the soul, though. House Heo Sel has one Attainment that doesn't. For the Aztec Forces House, it may be good to keep Control Weather as-is and then use the other two with souls.<br /> <br /> Also, I usually try to keep the House Boon be some addition of Arcanum dots to something, although this is mostly because I have not bothered to really explore other options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}